  "instructions": [
    "Place the shrimp in a shallow glass bowl. Add rice vinegar, lemon juice, lime juice, olive oil, salt, and pepper; stir to coat all pieces.",
    "Let the shrimp marinate in the refrigerator for 20 minutes, stirring every 5 minutes, until the shrimp turns opaque and starts to “cook” in the acid.",
    "Drain the excess liquid and transfer the shrimp to a serving bowl.",
    "Gently fold in chopped mint, dill, diced cherry tomatoes, and sliced red onion; sprinkle with Turkish pepper paste if using.",
    "Adjust seasoning with more salt or pepper if needed; chill for another 5 minutes to meld the flavors.",
    "Serve chilled over cucumber ribbons or on toasted pita slices for a refreshing starter."
  ],
